    "background_story": "Khai was a brilliant and ambitious surgeon who had always been fascinated by the complexities of the human digestive system. After years of rigorous training and research, he became a leading expert in gastroenterostomy, a surgical procedure that creates a new connection between the stomach and small intestine. Khai's innovative techniques and precision in the operating room earned him international recognition, and patients from around the world sought his expertise. One of his most notable cases was a young girl named Sophia, who had been born with a rare congenital defect that made it impossible for her to digest food normally. Khai's successful gastroenterostomy surgery gave Sophia a second chance at life, and she was finally able to eat and digest food like a normal child. Khai's dedication to his craft and his patients had a profound impact on the medical community, and his work continued to inspire a new generation of surgeons.",
